{"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","doc:\/\/Persistence\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Persistence\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore"]}],"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SegmentStore","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let store = try SegmentStore(events: [SignedUp.self, CheckedOut.self])","let tracker = Tracker(store: store)","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: vendor)"]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Write-through.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" A tracker’s worker writes each record as it reaches it, before publishing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it, with one "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"write()"},{"type":"text","text":", off the tracking caller’s thread, so the record survives the app"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"crashing or being killed from then on. The store makes the log durable against"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"power loss too ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fsync"},{"type":"text","text":") once per batch, before the batch is delivered, and whenever"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/synchronize()","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is called: call it, after the tracker’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flush()"},{"type":"text","text":", as the app moves to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"background or terminates."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A record whose write fails (the disk is full, say) is kept in memory only, and reported as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/writeFailed(recordCount:timestamps:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"What is kept.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Only events of the types in ","type":"text"},{"code":"events","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which conform to ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/BinaryCodable"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Events of any other type are kept in memory only: they are delivered in this run like any","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"other, are never written, and are lost if the app ends first. The first record of each such","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"type is reported as ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/notPersisted(event:)"},{"text":", so a type left out of ","type":"text"},{"code":"events","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"mistake shows up.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A record’s context is not kept: a recovered record is in the top-level ","type":"text"},{"code":"ServiceContext","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as its span ended with the earlier run.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Deleting."}]},{"type":"text","text":" A segment is deleted as a whole once every record in it is delivered, so a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"log whose records are all delivered holds no files. A segment kept for one undelivered"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record keeps its delivered ones too. Only recovery rewrites a segment: one still holding"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"records after it drops some ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/undecodable(recordCount:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/versionMismatch(event:storedVersion:currentVersion:recordCount:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rewritten without them, so each drop is reported once. Should the rewrite fail, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"segment is kept as it was and the next launch reports those drops again."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reading back."}]},{"type":"text","text":" When a destination’s full buffer drops a batch on its way through a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delivery, the delivery reads that batch’s records back from the log once the destination"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"has caught up, reading each segment they are in once, and hands them to it in this run,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each in the context it was tracked in, which the delivery keeps. A record the bound dropped"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"before the read finished isn’t read back, and one that can’t be read or decoded is logged"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and waits for a later launch."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Bound."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" The log never holds more than ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"byteBound"},{"text":" bytes. When a record wouldn’t fit, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"oldest segments are deleted until it does, and each one deleted with records not yet","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"delivered yields a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" on ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/dropReports","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". A record too large for an empty log","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is kept in memory only.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Recovery.","type":"text"}]},{"text":" A store opened on a directory recovers the records earlier runs left there","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and a tracker given the store delivers them first. Each segment is cut at its first torn or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"corrupt record, keeping every intact record before it, and the bytes cut off are reported.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A segment comes back whole, delivered records and all. Each record a delivery had started on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"comes back with ","type":"text"},{"code":"isRedelivered","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" set, as it may have reached a destination already: one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"delivered before the app ended, or one delivered just as it ended, before the store could","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"delete its segment. A record whose delivery mark can’t be written is held back from that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"delivery, so it is never sent twice unannounced, and delivered on a later launch.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Other versions."}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" A segment a newer release of the app wrote, in a later version of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"format, is left on disk untouched after a rollback, for that release to deliver: this one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"neither reads it nor counts it toward the bound. A segment in an earlier version, which this"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one can’t read, is deleted and reported as a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/corruption(byteCount:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Changed event types.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Each record’s event is a map of its properties by name, so a record","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"written before its type changed still reads: a property removed since is skipped, an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"optional one added since is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"text":" and one with a default value added since has it. A record","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"stored at another ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Event.schemaVersion"},{"text":" than its type’s now is dropped without being read and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reported as ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/versionMismatch(event:storedVersion:currentVersion:recordCount:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"One at the same version that can’t be read all the same, after a required property was added","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or a property’s type changed without raising the version, is dropped and reported as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/undecodable(recordCount:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Open one store per directory at a time; two would delete each other’s segments. Copies of a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"store share its log."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/init(events:directory:byteBound:segmentByteCount:)"],"anchor":"Initializers","generated":true,"title":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/byteCount","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/directory","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/dropReports","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/pendingRecordCount"],"anchor":"Instance-Properties","generated":true,"title":"Instance Properties"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/append(_:)","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/synchronize()","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/takeRecoveredRecords()"],"anchor":"Instance-Methods","generated":true,"title":"Instance Methods"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/defaultByteBound","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/defaultDirectory"],"anchor":"Type-Properties","generated":true,"title":"Type Properties"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" that keeps records in a directory of append-only segment files, bounded in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"size, until they are delivered."}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore"},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Persistence"}],"externalID":"s:11Persistence12SegmentStoreV","roleHeading":"Structure","title":"SegmentStore","remoteSource":{"fileName":"SegmentStore.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Persistence\/SegmentStore.swift#L69"},"symbolKind":"struct","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SegmentStore","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SegmentStore","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol"},"references":{"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/DropReport/writeFailed(recordCount:timestamps:)":{"title":"DropReport.writeFailed(recordCount:timestamps:)","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/dropreport\/writefailed(recordcount:timestamps:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"writeFailed"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"recordCount"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"timestamps"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ClosedRange","preciseIdentifier":"s:SN"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Date","preciseIdentifier":"s:20FoundationEssentials4DateV"},{"kind":"text","text":">)"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/writeFailed(recordCount:timestamps:)","abstract":[